The Iris Hour (art-nouveau demo): third-party assets

Library demo made by LemoLab × Claude Opus 5.5.

Fonts
- Cormorant Garamond (roman and italic, variable), by Christian Thalmann (Catharsis Fonts), SIL Open Font License 1.1.
  Source: https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/cormorantgaramond . Used for the subtitles. Files go in demo/fonts/ (not committed; download them as in TECHNIQUE section 11).

Voice
- Kokoro-82M via kokoro-onnx (voice af_nicole), Apache-2.0, https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx . Checked with faster-whisper (MIT).

Music and sound
- Score and foley are synthesised in code (demo/mix.py: Karplus-Strong harp and pizzicato, bowed cello, flute, celesta, bells, noise foley). No samples, no recordings.

Picture
- Everything (curves, flora, ornament, lettering skeletons, figure, paper texture) is generated in code in demo/engine/ and demo/show.js. No images, models or footage.
